{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh and Time-Step Coupling.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh and Time-Step Coupling.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mesh and time step coupling mesh and time step coupling","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh and Time-Step Coupling.md","fileName":"Mesh and Time-Step Coupling.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mesh and Time-Step Coupling","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Finite Element Thermal Modeling]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Finite Element Thermal Modeling","Mesh Independence Study","Time-Step Independence Study","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh and Time-Step Coupling.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh and Time-Step Coupling.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mesh and time step coupling mesh and time step coupling","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh and Time-Step Coupling.md","fileName":"Mesh and Time-Step Coupling.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mesh and Time-Step Coupling","heading":"Mesh and Time-Step Coupling","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Spatial element size and temporal step size jointly control a transient finite-element solution. A fine mesh cannot recover a rapid event skipped by coarse time steps, while very small time steps cannot resolve a steep spatial gradient on an inadequate mesh.\n\nBoth settings affect cost and convergence, and adaptive solvers may vary the actual step during a run. Separate [[Mesh Independence Study|mesh]] and [[Time-Step Independence Study|time-step]] checks help identify which discretization limits the accuracy of a reported peak or history.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Finite Element Thermal Modeling","Mesh Independence Study","Time-Step Independence Study","cos